  "provenance": {
    "physical_parameters": {
      "origin": "inferred",
      "note": "Ural-4320 YaMZ-238M2-style working variant; the engine in the user ZapSplat clip is unconfirmed. Manufacturer manual 236-3902150-B RE (2010), pp.6 and 30: V8, bore 130 mm, stroke 140 mm, compression ratio 16.5, firing order 1-5-4-2-6-3-7-8, nominal 2100 RPM, 550-650 RPM idle, static pump timing 15 deg BTDC. Hydraulic SOI is approximated by that setting; dynamic pump advance is not modeled. Full fuel mass 83 mg inferred from 96-100 mm3/cycle and assumed fuel density 850 kg/m3. Rod length, effective valve areas, thermal state and combustion coefficients are authored approximations. This is not a validated YaMZ pressure or torque model. Overlapping valve windows (intake 340-596 deg, exhaust 124-380 deg) and larger effective areas replace restrictive nonoverlapping audition values; window timing and effective-area profiles are authored, not verified from the reference vehicle."
    },
    "presentation": {
      "origin": "artistic",
      "note": "Authored heavy V8 block and exhaust transfer, intended for comparison with Ural-4320 recordings. Pole Position identifies its Ural recording as a 14.9-litre V8; that does not identify the engine or microphone position in the separate SmartSound/ZapSplat recording. No recording or measured transfer function is embedded. Fuel/cycle timing variation remains a playback approximation. Separate bank delay coloration, mass-flow-rate radiation, and authored flow-gated stochastic jet texture approximate an exhaust-microphone perspective; none are measured exhaust geometry or validated turbulent jet acoustics. Corrected Soundsnap public stream (90.7 s) and publisher startup previews guided acoustic tuning. A per-cylinder positive-rise envelope of fired minus motored pressure excites seeded stochastic block texture, with a separate coherent residual and compression contribution. Exhaust highpass, lossy bank reflections and lower-band flow texture are authored acoustic approximations; no reference PCM, waveform table or measured impulse response is embedded. No within-cycle crankshaft dynamics or physical turbulent flow is claimed."
    }
